  "scope": "The Kitty animation frame-composition suite alone in one ordinary (non-persistent, SessionPersistence Off) tab on a disposable macOS sidecar, the worker the App's own child: two cases (whole-frame a=c compositions that replace and blend, and refused compositions that change nothing), over paired original offscreen PNGs and complete cells/modes; the root's pixels are read back through the host decoder, the route a persistent session never takes. No stock collector ran, so there is no stock grade and no Core or common-harness claim; the pinned callbacks are replayed from the retained bundle and stay inconclusive by design. Not measured: a persistent tab in this publication (see the persistent one), rectangle offsets and sizes smaller than the image (pinned by unit tests; a partial composition is not one uniform color), a composition source or destination that is a PNG-encoded root (the root image is raw RGBA, f=32; only the added frame is PNG), a second client, remote sessions, other platforms.",
